  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Validating Plastic Waste Recycling in Guinee</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Waste collection and processing is a challenge in fast growing urban areas such as Conakry, Guinee. Plastic waste often ends up being burned at dumping sites, damaging the environment and increasing public health risks. The global production of plastics is growing rapidly whilst the production and use of recycled plastics is not keeping up with demand. Plastic recycling in Guinee is relatively new and the companies Touroul&#xe9; Nederland B.V. and Touroule Guinee aim to source and process used plastics from Guinee to offer these for further recycling purposes (upcycling). Technical Assistance (DGGF) provided support to prove commercial viability of collection, processing and shipping of 100,000 kg of shredded plastics from Guinee to the Netherlands. The project supported 11 direct jobs and approximately 120 indirect jobs &#x2013; mostly informal waste pickers &#x2013; and enabled knowledge transfer regarding by training 12 young people regarding plastic waste sorting and processing and created increased awareness amongst other stakeholders in the country. Furthermore, the project may lead to better plastic prices for informal local waste collectors by helping them add value.Further investments to expand the processing and sorting facility will be explored.</narrative>
  </description>
